[tt_bio.bindcraft2] stops at whichever comes first: 2 accepted designs, or 2 trajectories spent. Interleaved arms already running can carry the accepted count past 2, so it is a floor, not a quota.
[tt_bio.bindcraft2] a trajectory is also ended mid-design by the per-stage gates, which the campaign's own `filters` line does not list: screen pLDDT >= 0.6 (min_plddt_screen), refine pLDDT >= 0.6 (min_plddt_refine), anneal i_pTM >= 0.5 (min_iptm_anneal), anneal pLDDT >= 0.65 (min_plddt_anneal), harden i_pTM >= 0.5 (min_iptm_harden), harden pLDDT >= 0.65 (min_plddt_harden), mutate i_pTM >= 0.5 (min_iptm_mutate), mutate pLDDT >= 0.6 (min_plddt_mutate), final i_pTM >= 0.7 (min_iptm_final), final monomer pLDDT >= 0.7 (min_monomer_plddt_final), final pLDDT >= 0.7 (min_plddt_final). A trajectory that misses one is charged against the budget and counted under `terminated`, and the rejection names the metric (i_pTM/monomer pLDDT/pLDDT), not the setting.
